r:node3:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All five material outcomes are satisfied. The evidence directly establishes the initial topology and proof value, a coherent three-Sentinel deployment, authenticated TLS endpoints, functional protected credentials, and a complete disruption-promotion-write-restoration-resynchronization transition. Only minor temporary-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["The bounded disruption stopped Redis on node1 while leaving the host and its Sentinel running; whole-host and network-partition behavior were not tested.","Explicit negative authentication and transport tests were performed only against node2, although matching live configurations, certificates, listeners, and successful authenticated requests were observed on all three nodes.","No reboot persistence test was captured; services were directly observed active and enabled after recovery."]}
